osition with Two Female Nudes",1921,0,3,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,49],[136108493,"Composition",1938,0,3,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,50],[136548879,"Fischerboote",1913,0,3,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,51],[136826056,"Sans titre",1923,0,3,null,0,"3/37/Albert_Gleizes_Sans_titre_1923.jpeg/330px-Albert_Gleizes_Sans_titre_1923.jpeg",0,0,1,0,null],[137342306,"Figure gris-brun ou Figure gris-bleu",1952,0,3,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,52],[137718830,"Paysage",1911,0,3,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,21],[139074712,"L'homme dans la ville",1920,0,3,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,53],[141896551,"Composition",1922,0,3,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,54],[141976778,"Danseuse",1916,0,3,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[142276551,"Landscape",1912,0,3,null,0,"f/f7/Albert_Gleizes_-_Paisagem%2C_1912.jpg/330px-Albert_Gleizes_-_Paisagem%2C_1912.jpg",0,0,1,0,55]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaries":{"1362126":["Football Players is a 1912–13 painting by the French artist Albert Gleizes. The work was exhibited at the Salon des Indépendants, Paris, March–May 1913.","Football Players"],"5676845":["Le Dépiquage des Moissons, also known as Harvest Threshing, and The Harvesters, is an immense oil painting created in 1912 by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes (1881–1953).","Harvest Threshing"],"6529190":["The Bathers is a large oil painting created at the outset of 1912 by the French artist Albert Gleizes.","The Bathers (Gleizes)"],"16984914":["The Banks of the Marne is a proto-Cubist oil painting on canvas created in 1909 by the French artist Albert Gleizes. In this work can be seen a departure from the representation of the observable world.","The Banks of the Marne (Gleizes)"],"16985268":["Passy, Bridges of Paris, also called Les ponts de Paris (Passy), or Paysage à Passy, is a painting created in 1912 by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes.","Passy, Bridges of Paris"],"16986858":["The Hunt is a painting created in 1911 by the French artist Albert Gleizes.","The Hunt (Gleizes)"],"16986937":["Le Chemin, Paysage à Meudon, also known as Paysage avec personage, is an oil on canvas painted in 1911 by the artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes.","Le Chemin, Paysage à Meudon"],"17003030":["Woman with Phlox is an oil painting created in 1910 by the French artist Albert Gleizes. The painting was exhibited in Room 41 at the Salon des Indépendants in the Spring of 1911 ; the exhibition that introduced Cubism as a group manifestation to the general public for the first time.","Woman with Phlox"],"17009394":["Man on a Balcony, is a large oil painting created in 1912 by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes (1881–1953). The painting was exhibited in Paris at the Salon d'Automne of 1912.","Man on a Balcony"],"17014176":["The Publisher Eugène Figuière is a painting created by the French artist Albert Gleizes, from 1913. This work was exhibited at the Salon d'Automne, 1913 and Moderni Umeni, 45th Exhibition of SVU Mánes in Prague 1914, and several major exhibitions the following years.","The Publisher Eugène Figuière"],"17014184":["Portrait of Jacques Nayral is a large oil painting created in 1911 by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes (1881–1953).","Portrait of Jacques Nayral"],"17039555":["Woman with Animals, originally referred to as La dame aux bêtes and Portrait de Mme D.V. or Madame Raymond Duchamp-Villon, is a painting created late 1913 and completed during the month of February, 1914, by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes.","Woman with Animals"],"19882566":["Portrait of an Army Doctor is an oil-on-canvas painting created during 1914–15 by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes.","Portrait of an Army Doctor"],"19882569":["Composition for \"Jazz\", or Composition , is a 1915 painting by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes. This Cubist work was reproduced in a photograph of Gleizes working on the painting in the Xeic York Herald, then published in The Literary Digest, 27 November 1915 (p. 1225).","Composition for \"Jazz\""],"19882573":["Brooklyn Bridge is a 1915 painting by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes. Brooklyn Bridge was exhibited at the Montross Gallery, New York, 1916 along with works by Jean Crotti, Marcel Duchamp and Jean Metzinger.","Brooklyn Bridge (Gleizes)"],"22329841":["Woman with Black Glove is a painting by the French artist, theorist and writer Albert Gleizes.","Woman with Black Glove"],"52253497":["Cubist Landscape, also referred to as Tree and River and Paysage cubiste or Arbre et fleuve, is a Cubist painting created in 1914 by the French artist Albert Gleizes. Tree and River is one of Gleizes' last pre-World War I landscapes.","Cubist Landscape"],"77470212":["Man in a Hammock is a painting created by the French artist Albert Gleizes, from 1913. The work was exhibited at Moderni Umeni, SVU Mánes, Vystava, Prague, February – March 1914, no. 41; and Der Sturm, Berlin, July – August 1914.","Man in a Hammock"],"124022847":["The Tree, is a painting created in 1910 by the French artist Albert Gleizes.","The Tree (Gleizes)"]}}